## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end understanding of an AWS-based AI data flow, including extraction, NLP, storage, and indexing, plus privacy and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven design with S3, Lambda, Textract, Comprehend, DynamoDB
- IAM least privilege and KMS encryption
- Observability: DLQ, retries, CloudWatch
- Data governance: PII detection, versioning guidance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Lambda handler sketch
exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const s3Key = evt.Records[0].s3.object.key;
  const text = await textract.extractText(s3Key);
  const topics = await comprehend.classify(text);
  const pii = comprehend.detectPII(text);
  await s3.writeJSON(text, s3Key.replace('input','output'));
  await dynamo.upsert({ designId, s3Key, transcriptKey: '...', topics, piiFlag: pii > 0, timestamp: Date.now()});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale for 10k+ files/day?
- How would you validate privacy policies and redact data consistently?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design an end-to-end, real-time content workflow using SageMaker endpoints, with proper data security and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven AWS architectures
- S3 triggers, Lambda orchestration
- SageMaker endpoints for classification and NLP
- Data catalogs (DynamoDB), storage (S3)
- IAM, encryption, auditing, cost optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
// example: invoking SageMaker endpoint from Lambda (Node.js)
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const runtime = new AWS.SageMakerRuntime();
async function classify(text, endpoint){
  const res = await runtime.invokeEndpoint({EndpointName: endpoint, ContentType:'text/plain', Body: text}).promise();
  return JSON.parse(res.Body.toString())
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement idempotency and exactly-once processing for duplicate PUT events?
- How would you monitor latency and error rates, and what would you do to reduce cold start impacts?
